The first Windows snapshot was preserved unchanged. Its source NetCDF and upstream
commit were exact, but five target serializations differed by at most \(10^{-6}\)
log10 units because the upstream task applies NumPy log10 to float32. Recovery
recomputed only the declared transform from the exact raw float32 observations with
fixed precision and LF endings. The sealed split, gate, architecture, and hypothesis
were not changed.

Two initial full-flow attempts stopped before an epoch because MLflow rejected
conflicting serialization of a duplicated Lightning hyperparameter. A fast-development
probe also encountered Windows CP1252 output during MLflow finalization. Both software
defects were fixed, the failures remained logged, and the final six-run flow completed.
There was no OOM and no batch-size recovery was needed.

\section{Failure analysis and limitations}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Hypothesis failure.} Persistence beats both neural families. This likely
reflects the strength of local temporal continuity and the inadequacy of the current
sequence representation across irregular gaps; the result does not justify a causal claim.
\item \textbf{MLP scale saturation.} Hard clamping permits the Gaussian scale to stick at
its maximum, yielding enormous intervals and the formal overcoverage failure.
\item \textbf{Strata-OT bias.} Both seeds have negative bias around -0.35 log10 units,
correlation below 0.63, and undercoverage below 45\%.
\item \textbf{Single-site scope.} No vertical layers, integrated optical metrics,
cross-site OOD behavior, propagation-path performance, or selective-risk curves are
supported by this surface point task. Such metrics are reported as unsupported, not zero.
\item \textbf{Irregular time.} Context length counts surviving rows, not fixed elapsed
time, after dropna gaps. A time-gap-aware sequence model is needed before interpreting
attention as a physical history.
\item \textbf{Reproducibility boundary.} The checkout had no Git commit. Exact training
source is therefore preserved as a content-addressed archive and all runs record the
dirty state, digest, data hashes, split hash, configuration, environment, predictions,
plots, checkpoints, runtime, and VRAM.
\end{itemize}

